{#
compose/_template_panel.html.twig
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
The compose window's template picker: a list to choose from, a preview of
whichever row the pointer or the focus is on, and two ways out at the foot.

Fetched into the dropdown each time it opens (see _window.html.twig for why it
is not rendered with the window) and driven by compose--template-picker, which
is on the dropdown's wrapper — this fragment declares targets and actions for
it and no controller of its own.

ORDER. The account being written from comes first, because that is where the
template for this message most likely is. Then the top level, which belongs to
no account. Then everything else, under its own headings: filed elsewhere, but
still the user's, and still one click away.

Inside a group the folders are flattened, each template carrying its folder's
name at the right. A tree with disclosure triangles in a 13rem column of a
dropdown is a tree nobody can aim at; the search field is how a long list is
navigated here.

EACH ROW CARRIES ITS OWN PREVIEW, as the stored subject and body, tokens and
all. The controller draws the tokens as the same chips the editor draws
(template_variables.js), so the preview shows what the template IS — which
variable goes where — and the inserted message shows what it became. The body
is in a <template> element so the browser parses it without rendering it or
loading anything it refers to.

Variables:
  tree        App\Domain\DTO\Template\TemplateTree
  current     Account|null  the account in From
  chipLabels  see TemplateEditorViewData::chipLabels()
#}
{% macro rows(templates, folder) %}
    {% for template in templates %}
        <li>
            <button type="button"
                    data-compose--template-picker-target="item"
                    data-url="{{ path('app_compose_templates_render', { id: template.id }) }}"
                    data-name="{{ template.name|lower }}"
                    data-subject="{{ template.subject }}"
                    data-action="click->compose--template-picker#choose mouseenter->compose--template-picker#preview focus->compose--template-picker#preview"
                    class="flex w-full items-center gap-2 min-h-9 md:min-h-8 px-2 py-1 rounded-lg text-sm text-left
                           text-ink-muted hover:bg-hover hover:text-ink focus:bg-hover focus:text-ink focus:outline-none
                           transition-colors cursor-pointer">
                <i class="fa-regular fa-file-lines w-4 text-center text-ink-faint shrink-0" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                <span class="truncate flex-1 min-w-0">{{ template.name }}</span>
                {% if folder %}
                    <span class="shrink-0 max-w-[40%] truncate text-[11px] text-ink-faint">{{ folder }}</span>
                {% endif %}
                <template>{{ template.body|raw }}</template>
            </button>
        </li>
    {% endfor %}
{% endmacro %}

{% macro group(node, heading) %}
    {% if node.total > 0 %}
        <li data-compose--template-picker-target="group">
            <p class="px-2 pt-2 pb-1 text-[11px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-ink-faint truncate">{{ heading }}</p>
            <ul>
                {% for folder in node.flattened %}
                    {{ _self.rows(folder.templates, folder.depth > 0 ? folder.name : null) }}
                {% endfor %}
            </ul>
        </li>
    {% endif %}
{% endmacro %}

<div data-compose--template-picker-target="root"
     data-chip-labels="{{ chipLabels|json_encode|e('html_attr') }}"
     data-csrf="{{ csrf_token('template_save_draft') }}"
     class="md:grid md:grid-cols-[13.5rem_minmax(0,1fr)]">

    <div class="min-w-0 p-1.5 md:border-r border-line">
        {% if tree.empty %}
            <p class="px-2 py-6 text-center text-sm text-ink-faint">{{ 'compose.template.empty'|trans }}</p>
        {% else %}
            <label class="flex items-center gap-2 h-8 px-2 rounded-lg border border-field bg-field text-ink-faint">
                <i class="fa-solid fa-magnifying-glass text-[11px]" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                <input type="search"
                       data-compose--template-picker-target="search"
                       data-action="input->compose--template-picker#filter"
                       placeholder="{{ 'compose.template.search'|trans }}"
                       aria-label="{{ 'compose.template.search'|trans }}"
                       class="flex-1 min-w-0 bg-transparent text-sm text-ink placeholder:text-ink-faint focus:outline-none">
            </label>

            <ul class="mt-1 max-h-64 overflow-y-auto">
                {% for node in tree.accounts %}
                    {% if current is not null and node.location.account is same as(current) %}
                        {{ _self.group(node, node.name) }}
                    {% endif %}
                {% endfor %}

                {% if tree.templates|length %}
                    <li data-compose--template-picker-target="group">
                        <p class="px-2 pt-2 pb-1 text-[11px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-ink-faint">
                            {{ 'compose.template.all_accounts'|trans }}
                        </p>
                        <ul>{{ _self.rows(tree.templates, null) }}</ul>
                    </li>
                {% endif %}

                {% for node in tree.accounts %}
                    {% if current is null or node.location.account is not same as(current) %}
                        {{ _self.group(node, node.name) }}
                    {% endif %}
                {% endfor %}
                {% for node in tree.folders %}
                    {{ _self.group(node, node.name) }}
                {% endfor %}
            </ul>

            <p data-compose--template-picker-target="noMatch" hidden
               class="px-2 py-4 text-center text-sm text-ink-faint">{{ 'compose.template.no_match'|trans }}</p>
        {% endif %}
    </div>

    {# The preview. Hidden below md: there a row is tapped, not hovered, and a
       tap inserts — a pane that only ever shows the template you have just
       inserted is a pane showing you the message. #}
    <div class="hidden md:flex flex-col min-w-0 p-3">
        <p data-compose--template-picker-target="previewSubject"
           class="pl-var-preview text-sm font-semibold text-ink break-words"></p>
        <div data-compose--template-picker-target="previewBody"
             class="pl-var-preview mt-1.5 max-h-56 overflow-y-auto text-xs leading-relaxed text-ink-soft"></div>
    </div>

    <div class="md:col-span-2 flex items-center justify-between gap-3 px-3 py-2 border-t border-line bg-sunken">
        <button type="button"
                data-action="click->compose--template-picker#saveDraft"
                class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs text-ink-muted hover:text-ink transition-colors cursor-pointer">
            <i class="fa-regular fa-floppy-disk" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            {{ 'compose.template.save_draft'|trans }}
        </button>
        {# _top: this fragment lives inside the compose frame, and a link
           followed in there would try to load the settings page into the
           dock. #}
        <a href="{{ path('app_settings_index', { section: 'templates' }) }}"
           data-turbo-frame="_top"
           class="text-xs text-accent hover:underline">{{ 'compose.template.manage'|trans }}</a>
    </div>
</div>
